 (J1 at 180 deg, R1, C1, GND symbols, PWR_FLAG) in inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_sch; confirmed J1.1=/IN, J1.2=/OUT, J1.3=GND, R1 between /IN and /OUT, C1 between /OUT and GND, matching work/netlist/design.xml and work/netlist/connectivity.json.\",\"Cross-checked all 7 board pad net assignments in inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb against the netlist (R1.1=/IN, R1.2=/OUT, C1.1=/OUT, C1.2=GND, J1.1=/IN, J1.2=/OUT, J1.3=GND): consistent.\",\"Traced copper connectivity on the board: /IN segment (100,100)-(104.0875,100) joins J1.1 to R1.1; /OUT segments join R1.2 to C1.1 and J1.2 via the T-junction at (107.5,100) onto the y=100 /OUT segment; GND segment (110.95,100)-(113,100) joins C1.2 to the 0.6/0.3 mm via; J1.3 ground return closes on the B.Cu GND zone through saved thermal-relief spokes visible in the filled_polygon.\",\"Verified geometry criterion directly from the native board file: all 5 track segments are width 0.25 mm >= 0.2 mm declared minimum, matching work/geometry/geometry.json (narrowest 0.25 mm); via (0.6 mm) and zone (min_thickness 0.25 mm, thermal_bridge_width 0.5 mm) also exceed 0.2 mm though not formally in scope of the track-segment requirement.\",\"Verified the simulation deck work/rc-step/deck.cir against the netlist and values (C1 OUT 0 100n, R1 IN OUT 10k, GND mapped to node 0, J1 correctly excluded as element-free connector); stimulus PWL(0 0 1n 1) is a valid ideal-step approximation; .tran 0.005m 5m gives adequate resolution for tau=1 ms.\",\"Recomputed the analytic response: tau = 10k * 100n = 1.0 ms; V(1 ms) = 1-exp(-1) = 0.6321206 V vs measured 0.6321201 V (within declared 0.62-0.65 V band); V(5 ms) = 1-exp(-5) = 0.9932621 V vs measured 0.9932621 V. ngspice.log measurement lines match the reported check details.\",\"Confirmed board outline containment: all footprints, tracks, via (113,100) and zone (96.5-115.5 x 96.5-107.5) lie within the Edge.Cuts rectangle (96-116 x 96-108).\",\"Reviewed ERC and DRC records (work/erc/erc.json, work/drc/drc.json): zero violations, zero unconnected items, zero parity issues; ignored-check lists are benign for this all-passive design; PWR_FLAG on GND is correctly placed for ERC.\",\"Checked that the unconstrained vout_5ms measurement is consistent with inputs/requirements/fixture-requirements.md, which bounds only the 1 ms point.\"],\"limitations\":[\"work/rc-step/result.raw is binary and was not readable in this packet; waveform verification rests on ngspice.log measurement lines plus analytic recomputation.\",\"B.Cu zone connectivity (J1.3 ground return) was verified from the saved filled_polygon geometry and the DRC/geometry unconnected-items counts, not by an independent refill or geometric recomputation of spoke widths; the read-only candidate forbids a refill pass.\",\"Tolerance, temperature, external loading, ADC sampling, EMI and physical hardware behavior are outside the declared operating conditions and were not assessed, per the fixture's stated scope.\",\"Footprint internal correctness (pad-to-land suitability of the stock KiCad 0805 and pin-header footprints) is taken from the standard library definitions embedded in the board file; no manufacturer land-pattern comparison was in scope.\"],\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"geom-probe-assert-noise\",\"title\":\"Geometry probe emitted wxWidgets assertion failures on console despite exit 0\",\"location\":\"work/geometry/console.log\",\"condition\":\"The geometry probe console log contains three repeated assertion messages: 'assert \\\"m_choices.GetCount() > 0\\\" failed in PROPERTY_ENUM(): No enum choices defined', alongside the normal summary line, while execution.json records exit_code 0.\",\"mechanism\":\"Internal library assertions during a measurement run indicate the tool exercised an unexpected code path; a successful exit is not by itself proof the reported measurements are trustworthy, so the probe output needed independent confirmation.\",\"severity\":\"info\",\"assessment\":\"concern\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/geometry/console.log\",\"locator\":\"lines 2-4 (property.h(607) assert messages)\"},{\"path\":\"work/geometry/execution.json\",\"locator\":\"exit_code: 0, stderr_sha256 ecfdabc9...\"},{\"path\":\"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb\",\"locator\":\"segment blocks: all five (segment ... (width 0.25)) entries, uuids ae12bf6f, 69a2edc1, 8b528360, a6dab0b4, 7deb1fb0\"}],\"reasoning\":\"I independently read every track segment in the native board file: all five are 0.25 mm wide, matching the probe's reported narrowest 0.25 mm and segment count of 5, so the geometry verdict stands despite the assertion noise. Logged as an informational concern about tool health only; it does not change the pass result.\"},{\"id\":\"gnd-return-single-path\",\"title\":\"Connector ground return depends entirely on saved zone fill and one 0.3 mm-drill via\",\"location\":\"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb (via b71a70d7 at 113,100; zone 38a83012 on B.Cu)\",\"condition\":\"There is no F.Cu copper between J1 pad 3 (GND, at 100,105.08) and C1 pad 2 (GND); the only ground path is C1.2 -> 2.05 mm track -> single via (0.6 mm pad / 0.3 mm drill) -> B.Cu GND zone -> thermal-relief spokes into J1.3. The zone fill is evaluated as saved and a refill pass is forbidden.\",\"mechanism\":\"If the saved fill were stale relative to an edited outline or clearance, or the single via failed in fabrication, the GND net would open with no redundant path; connectivity evidence here is the saved filled_polygon plus DRC/geometry unconnected counts of zero.\",\"severity\":\"info\",\"assessment\":\"concern\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb\",\"locator\":\"via (at 113 100) (size 0.6) (drill 0.3) net GND; zone net GND layer B.Cu with filled_polygon thermal spokes around (100,105.08), e.g. points (xy 99.517037 104.950591)...(xy 100.482962 104.95059)\"},{\"path\":\"work/drc/drc.json\",\"locator\":\"unconnected_items: [] (count 0)\"},{\"path\":\"work/geometry/geometry.json\",\"locator\":\